-- #847 phase 2 (lane X, 2026-10-21): Pandaria (map 870) in the bot travel graph (playerbots DB; beyond AC - ACs
-- graph is 3.3.5 data and had no node on map 870, so a roaming bot in Pandaria never got a node route).
--
-- Built offline the way ACs TravelNodeMap generator builds a map (TravelNode.cpp generateNpcNodes /
-- generateAreaTriggerNodes / generateWalkPaths / removeUselessPaths / generateTaxiPaths / removeLowNodes), over the
-- servers own data (mmaps + DBCs, world DB):
--  - one node per 5.4.8 innkeeper / flight master spawn on map 870 (named <area> innkeeper / <area> flightMaster
--    like AC; a spawn within 5 yd of a node reuses it), placed on the nearest walkable poly of the main navmesh
--    component (within 12 yd of the spawn);
--  - walk links (type 1) between every two nodes within 2000 yd that the navmesh connects: Detour A* with the bot
--    filter (ground + water, water area cost 20), funnel, points every <= 15 yd, both directions; AC calculateCost
--    values (distance from 0.1, swim distance, max creature levels of the 5.4.8 spawns within 50 yd); then ACs
--    isUselessLink crop (a link is dropped when going via a neighbour is < 1.1x as long);
--  - flight-path links (type 4) for every TaxiPath.dbc path whose two TaxiNodes have a node within 15 yd
--    (distance 0.1, extra cost = path length / 3600, the TaxiPathNode points as the path; replaces a walk link);
--  - portal links (type 2, distance 0.1, extra cost 3, path = entrance + exit, as ACs area-trigger portals):
--    Stormwind -> Pawdon Village and Orgrimmar -> Honeydew Village (the 5.4.8 phased portals, gameobjects;
--    their spells have no destination row, so the exit is the village inn node), and the Shrine of Seven Stars /
--    Two Moons portals back to the Stormwind / Orgrimmar arrival point of the Cata zone portals (84505 / 84506).
--    A portal link teleports the bot (NewRpgRoamTransport.cpp NODE_PORTAL), the gameobject is not used.
-- Ids 3800-3999 (the test DB ends at 3779, lane F 846 uses 3780-3785). Every row is linked / calculated = 1, so
-- TravelNodeMap::LoadOrGenerate keeps the stored graph (no regeneration at boot).
-- Apply after 2026_10_21_laneF_846.sql and 2026_10_21_laneX_847_phase1.sql.
-- Generator: gen_region.py 2, emit_region.py 2.
-- Undo: the three DELETEs at the end of this header (every row of this file has an id in 3800-3999).
-- DELETE FROM `playerbots_travelnode_link` WHERE `node_id` BETWEEN 3800 AND 3999 OR `to_node_id` BETWEEN 3800 AND 3999;
-- DELETE FROM `playerbots_travelnode_path` WHERE `node_id` BETWEEN 3800 AND 3999 OR `to_node_id` BETWEEN 3800 AND 3999;
-- DELETE FROM `playerbots_travelnode` WHERE `id` BETWEEN 3800 AND 3999;
